  "Question": "Lines \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are cut by line \\(c\\). Angles \\(\\angle 1\\) and \\(\\angle 2\\) are same-side interior angles, and \\(\\angle 1=75^\\circ\\). What must the measure of \\(\\angle 2\\) be, in degrees, for \\(a\\parallel b\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "105",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "If same-side interior angles are supplementary, the two lines are parallel, so \\(\\angle 2=180^\\circ-75^\\circ=105^\\circ\\).",
